(6620974, 987879, 59029, '<td valign="top">Great use of a hairy scary spider laying in wait in the dark!  However, I feel that the overexposed rest of the pic is a turnoff for the more technical voters.  That, and the fact that said cause of fear is a spider, and sadly the odds are probably not in your favour.  Still, gave you an 8.</td>', 'Great use of a hairy scary spider laying in wait in the dark!  However, I feel that the overexposed rest of the pic is a turnoff for the more technical voters.  That, and the fact that said cause of fear is a spider, and sadly the odds are probably not in your favour.  Still, gave you an 8.', '2011-12-18 20:31:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6620990, 988663, 124982, '<td valign="top">Hi Susan, really liked the composition of this one. Definitely a good entry that fits the title of the song (which happens to be one of my all-time faves!!) very well! Also, the lighting (looks to be a fire?) really gives it a mysterious and ominous feel that once again fits the challenge.<br/> <br/>The <i>only</i> thing I feel didn''t really work was the method of processing. The mans'' skin seems to have heavy artifacting? I''m guessing it''s what you were going for, but not sure how it contributes to the image? It''s a little weird, and may work against you by the "purist" voters.<br/> <br/>Overall, a great entry...hope it''s doing well for you!</td>', 'Hi Susan, really liked the composition of this one. Definitely a good entry that fits the title of the song (which happens to be one of my all-time faves!!) very well! Also, the lighting (looks to be a fire?) really gives it a mysterious and ominous feel that once again fits the challenge. The only thing I feel didn''t really work was the method of processing. The mans'' skin seems to have heavy artifacting? I''m guessing it''s what you were going for, but not sure how it contributes to the image? It''s a little weird, and may work against you by the "purist" voters. Overall, a great entry...hope it''s doing well for you!', '2011-12-18 21:10:55.000000', NULL, 1),
